    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d715">

                <pb facs="0839" n="827" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg827"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390.1115A/1285: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-11-17">November 17, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2573. American interests—Far East internees. Your 4994, November 5th,<anchor
                        n="65" xml:id="d715-f1"/> and 5069, November 9th.<anchor n="66"
                        xml:id="d715-f2"/> Request Swiss Government and Intercross<anchor n="66a"
                        xml:id="d715-f3"/> Committee to have their representatives visit all
                    Americans now or in future interned occupied China and endeavor to expedite
                    transmission weekly lists names and information regarding addresses, health, et
                    cetera as provided in Article 77 of Geneva Convention.</p>
                <p>Keep Department currently informed regarding developments this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d715-f1" n="65" xml:id="d715-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported that Japanese authorities at Hankow, Tsingtao, and
                    Chefoo had assembled all citizens of countries at war with Japan in certain
                    groups of houses and were considering their internment at Shanghai and elsewhere
                    in occupied China (390.1115A/1279).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d715-f2" n="66" xml:id="d715-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported that Japanese police in Shanghai had arrested about 100
                    citizens of countries at war with Japan.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d715-f3" n="66a" xml:id="d715-f3-content">
                <p>International Red Cross.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
